    z96a dt: free GPIO0_C1 from sdio-pwrseq, force vcc3v3_lcd0_n always-on (WiFi main power fix)
    
    Root cause of WiFi SDIO enumeration failure (Pin 36 VDD_3.3V = 0V,
    measured by multimeter):
    
    sdio-pwrseq.pinctrl-0 referenced wifi-enable-h (GPIO0_C1/pin17),
    which claims the pin as a GPIO function that the pwrseq driver
    never drives. Meanwhile vcc3v3_lcd0_n uses the SAME pin as its
    enable-active-high GPIO. Result: the 3.3V LDO enable pin floats,
    WiFi module main power never comes up, CMD5 gets no response,
    mmc2 gives up and WL_REG_ON (gpio-16) stays low.
    
    Fix:
    1. Remove pinctrl-names/pinctrl-0 from sdio-pwrseq. The pwrseq
       driver only needs reset-gpios (gpio-16); it never touches C1.
    2. Add regulator-always-on to vcc3v3_lcd0_n so the 3.3V LDO is
       force-enabled regardless of boot sequencing.
    
    Verified safe4 baseline retained: sc8886 disabled, OTP clock-names,
    battery okay, dwmmc normal/idle pinctrl, gpu-thermal trips.

